35,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"I'm afraid the budget is tighter than we thought, and off-site work brings in no revenue.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shion,,"Previous trials showed real patient benefit, but logistical failures in the field are a recurring theme.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Midori,,"We have a serious shortage of ward nurses, but the midwifery team actually has some unexpected capacity.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"The car park is full by eleven! And if it's not a fixed appointment, the system doesn't even see it.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shizue,,It seems we struggle when we rely on others or shared responsibilities without clear ownership.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Midori, the midwifery slack is interesting, but we must consider the funding source.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Kenji, your point about the booking system explains why some initiatives seem to vanish.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Jonathan, if we use existing slack, we might avoid adding pressure to the struggling ward nurses.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"If we do something at home, we don't need the car park, right?","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"But @Kenji, my findings show that home visits are often missed due to simple obstacles.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"Exactly. And since off-site visits earn nothing, they are a financial drain on a shrinking budget.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shion,,"We need a program that is recordable, sustainable, and utilizes available staff without overloading the site.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Midori,,A program involving midwifery could work well given their current capacity.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Kenji,,So something on-site but not taking up too many rooms? Or something that doesn't need the shuttle?,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shizue,,We must avoid joint ventures where no one takes responsibility for the budget or rota.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,On-site programs are more financially viable due to the tariffs.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shion,,Agreed. The data suggests we should avoid high-risk external dependencies.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Midori,,I feel a perinatal service would be a gentle way to use our available resources.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Kenji,,As long as it fits in the booking system and doesn't break the car park!,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shizue,,Let us see the candidates and ensure the responsibility is clearly defined.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
